### Ecom API Tests
### Make sure your server is running: make run

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@apiUrl = {{baseUrl}}/api/v1
@token =

### Health Check - Test if server is running
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

###

### API Test - Test basic API functionality  
# GET {{apiUrl}}/test

###

### User Registration - Valid data
POST {{apiUrl}}/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "firstName": "John",
    "lastName": "Doe",
    "email": "john.doe@example.com",
    "password": "password123"
}

###

### User Registration - Different user
POST {{apiUrl}}/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "firstName": "Jane",
    "lastName": "Smith", 
    "email": "jane.smith@example.com",
    "password": "mypassword456"
}

###

### User Registration - Invalid data (should fail validation)
POST {{apiUrl}}/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "firstName": "",
    "lastName": "",
    "email": "invalid-email",
    "password": "123"
}

###

### User Registration - Duplicate email (should fail with conflict)
POST {{apiUrl}}/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "firstName": "Another",
    "lastName": "John",
    "email": "john.doe@example.com",
    "password": "differentpassword"
}

###

### User Login 
POST {{apiUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "john.doe@example.com",
    "password": "password123"
}

###

### Get Products 
# GET {{apiUrl}}/products

###

### Create Product
POST {{apiUrl}}/products
Content-Type: application/json
# Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
    "name": "iPhone 15",
    "description": "Latest Apple smartphone",
    "price": 999.99,
    "quantity": 50
}
# POST {{apiUrl}}/products
# Content-Type: application/json
# Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
# 
# {
#     "name": "iPhone 15",
#     "description": "Latest Apple smartphone",
#     "price": 999.99,
